{"openapi":"3.0.3","info":{"title":"Fluen Studio API Reference","description":"This API, organized around REST principles, allows clients to upload audio or video files through a media creation endpoint, along with their transcription and translation job specifications, or to import subtitles they already have (SRT) for translation without uploading any media file. Subtitles corrected outside Fluen can be re-imported into an existing caption track (see Import Track Content), replacing its content and optionally restarting the translations in one call. Following processing, the transcribed and translated subtitle tracks can be retrieved, exported in all common subtitle formats, or burned into the video to produce an MP4 with hardcoded subtitles (a 'burn-in', which the web app calls an MP4 export). Webhooks report every job the moment it finishes, so no polling is needed.\n\n## Authentication\n\nThe API uses API key authentication. To obtain an API key:\n\n1. Log in to your Fluen Studio account\n2. Navigate to 'My Account' > 'API & Webhooks'\n3. Click on 'Generate Secret Key'\n4. Copy and store the secret key securely - it will only be shown once\n\nInclude your API key in all requests using the `X-API-Key` header. The API key gives you access to operate on all your workspaces and their associated assets.\n\n**Important**: Keep your API key secure and never share it publicly. If you suspect your API key has been compromised, you can revoke it and generate a new one from the same page.\n## Captions, review, and translations\n\nBy default, captions created through the API complete on their own and any translations\nrequested with them (or added later) start immediately: expect `caption.completed`\nfollowed by `translation.completed` with no action needed in between.\n\nTeams that want captions reviewed by an editor before translation can pass\n`captionPostEdit: true` when creating the media. The caption track then waits in\n`POST_EDIT` status after transcription, and translations stay `SCHEDULED` until the\ncaptions are approved in the web editor. Approval is a web action; plan for it in\nyour workflow before enabling the flag.\n\nAlready have subtitles? The \"Create Media from captions\" operation builds a\ncaptions-only media from an inline SRT: no upload and no transcription runs, and the\ncaption track is ready immediately. Add translation languages to it and export the\nresults. Translations are billed on the SRT's duration; the imported captions are free.\n\n## Webhooks\n\nEvery Fluen job (encode, transcription, translation, burn-in) runs asynchronously and takes\nanywhere from a few seconds to a few minutes to finish. Instead of polling\n`GET /api/media/{mediaId}`, register a **webhook endpoint**\nand Fluen will `POST` a signed JSON event to your URL the moment a job reaches a terminal state.\n\nManage endpoints with the `/api/webhook-endpoints` operations: register a URL plus an event-type\nfilter, list, update, delete, rotate the signing secret, send a test ping, and inspect recent\ndeliveries. The signing secret is shown only once, at creation and on rotate-secret. Each user\ncan have at most 50 active endpoints.\n\nPayloads are outbound and so do not appear as operations in this reference. The event catalog,\npayload shape, and signature scheme below are the stable contract: field names are additive and\nare never renamed once shipped.\n\n### Event catalog\n\n| Event type | Fired when | Key `data` fields |\n|---|---|---|\n| `media.ready` | media finished encoding | `mediaId`, `mediaTitle`, `workspaceId`, `status`, `durationMs`, `mediaType` |\n| `media.failed` | encode or source-URL import failed | the above, plus `errorMessage` |\n| `caption.completed` | a transcription track completed | `mediaId`, `mediaTitle`, `workspaceId`, `trackId`, `languageId`, `jobType`, `status` |\n| `caption.failed` | a transcription failed | the above, plus `reason` (e.g. `INSUFFICIENT_CREDITS`) |\n| `translation.completed` | a translation track completed (one event per language) | `mediaId`, `mediaTitle`, `workspaceId`, `trackId`, `languageId`, `jobType`, `status` |\n| `translation.failed` | a translation track failed | the above, plus `reason` |\n| `burnin.completed` | a subtitle burn-in finished | `burnInId`, `mediaId`, `mediaTitle`, `workspaceId`, `trackId`, `videoFormat`, `status` |\n| `burnin.failed` | a subtitle burn-in failed | the above, plus `errorMessage` |\n\nA synthetic `ping` event is sent only by the test-endpoint operation and is never matched by a\nsubscription.\n\n### Payload\n\nEvery delivery is an HTTP `POST` with `Content-Type: application/json` and this envelope:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"evt_9f2c4e1abd7e4f0e8a1c6b5d4e3f2a10\",\n  \"type\": \"translation.completed\",\n  \"apiVersion\": \"2026-07-01\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-07-10T14:12:09.482913Z\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"mediaId\": \"aB3xK9\",\n    \"mediaTitle\": \"Q3 townhall.mp4\",\n    \"workspaceId\": \"ws_7Yn2\",\n    \"trackId\": \"trk_Fr8\",\n    \"languageId\": \"fr\",\n    \"jobType\": \"TRANSLATION\",\n    \"status\": \"COMPLETE\"\n  },\n  \"links\": {\n    \"media\": \"https://api.fluen.ai/api/media/aB3xK9\",\n    \"track\": \"https://api.fluen.ai/api/tracks/trk_Fr8\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n`id` is stable across retries of the same event: use it to deduplicate. `links` are absolute\nURLs to the canonical resources (`GET`), present when the event has a media/track. What you *do*\nwith a track (export it or burn it in) is a separate call (see below), not a link. Each\ndelivery also carries these headers:\n\n| Header | Value |\n|---|---|\n| `X-Fluen-Event` | the event type, e.g. `translation.completed` |\n| `X-Fluen-Delivery` | id of this delivery attempt-series |\n| `X-Fluen-Signature` | `t=<unix-seconds>,v1=<hex hmac-sha256>`; see below |\n\n### Acting on an event\n\nThe `mediaId` / `trackId` in `data` are the durable handles. Common follow-ups:\n\n- **Export a track** in any supported format: `GET /api/tracks/{trackId}/export/{format}`, where\n  `{format}` is one of `SRT`, `VTT`, `TXT`, `DOCX`, `PDF`, `SSA`, `TTML`, `ITT`, `SBV`, `STL`\n  (uppercase: the value binds case-sensitively).\n- **Burn subtitles into the video**, producing an MP4 with hardcoded subtitles (what the web app\n  calls an MP4 export; the API calls it a burn-in). This is a job, not a plain download:\n  `POST /api/tracks/{trackId}/burnin/{videoFormat}` with no body (or `{}`) to render the track's\n  saved style, `{videoFormat}` one of `ORIGINAL`, `HIGHEST`, `HIGH`, `STANDARD` (see the operation\n  for what each resolution means). Wait for the `burnin.completed` event (or poll\n  `GET /api/tracks/{trackId}/burnin`), then fetch a time-limited download URL from\n  `GET /api/tracks/{trackId}/burnin/{burnInId}/download`.\n\n### Verifying signatures\n\nEach delivery is signed with your endpoint's secret so you can confirm it came from Fluen and was\nnot altered in transit. The `X-Fluen-Signature` header is `t=<timestamp>,v1=<signature>`, where the\nsignature is `HMAC-SHA256(secret, \"<timestamp>.<raw-body>\")` rendered as lowercase hex.\n\nTo verify: recompute the HMAC over `timestamp + \".\" + rawBody` with your secret and compare it to\n`v1` in constant time. Also reject deliveries whose timestamp is far from your clock: the\ntimestamp is bound into the signature to prevent replay.\n\n```javascript\nconst crypto = require('crypto');\n\nfunction verifyFluenWebhook(rawBody, signatureHeader, secret) {\n  const parts = Object.fromEntries(signatureHeader.split(',').map(kv => kv.split('=')));\n  const expected = crypto.createHmac('sha256', secret)\n    .update(parts.t + '.' + rawBody)\n    .digest('hex');\n  const signatureOk = parts.v1.length === expected.length &&\n    crypto.timingSafeEqual(Buffer.from(parts.v1), Buffer.from(expected));\n  const fresh = Math.abs(Date.now() / 1000 - Number(parts.t)) < 300; // 5-minute tolerance\n  return signatureOk && fresh;\n}\n```\n\nVerify against the exact raw request body, before any JSON parsing or re-serialization.\n\n### Delivery, retries, and hygiene\n\n- **At-least-once.** A retry can re-deliver an event you already received; deduplicate on the\n  envelope `id`.\n- **Success** is any `2xx` within a 10-second timeout. Anything else, including timeouts and\n  connection errors, is a failed attempt.\n- **Retries** back off over roughly five hours: 30s, 2m, 10m, 1h, 4h (five retries after the first\n  attempt), after which the delivery is abandoned.\n- **410 Gone.** If your endpoint responds `410`, the subscription is deactivated immediately with\n  no retries (REST Hooks convention). Return `410` when the receiving hook no longer exists.\n- **Auto-disable.** After 15 consecutive abandoned deliveries an endpoint is disabled and its owner\n  emailed; re-enable it with the update operation. This stops dead URLs from being retried forever.\n- **Retention.** Delivery records stay queryable via the deliveries operation for 30 days.\n- Only `https` URLs are accepted, and any URL resolving to a private or reserved IP range is\n  rejected at registration and again at delivery time.\n\n### Zapier and Make\n\nEndpoints follow the REST Hooks pattern, so Zapier instant triggers work directly (Zapier\nsubscribes by creating an endpoint and unsubscribes by deleting it). The\n`GET /api/webhook-endpoints/sample-events?type=<event-type>` operation returns recent real events,\nor a representative example, so Zap builders can map fields before a live event fires. Make.com\n\"custom webhook\" triggers consume the same payloads.\n\n## Free trial plan limits\n\nEvery plan, including the free one, can create API keys and use the full API surface\nand webhooks. Free accounts are limited in the number of successful jobs they can run,\nand their translations may be only partial. When a plan limit is reached, the API\nresponds `402` (or `403` for unavailable features) with code `FREE_TIER_LIMIT` and a\nmessage that states the exact limit and carries an upgrade link; asynchronous jobs\nreport plan-limit failures through the failure webhooks' `reason` field (e.g.\n`FREE_DURATION_LIMIT`). A partial translation carries `isPartial: true` and can be\ncompleted after upgrading. Building or testing an integration and need more room than\nthe free plan allows? Email support@fluen.ai and tell us what you are working on.\n\n## Errors and rate limits\n\nError responses carry a JSON body with a machine-readable `code`, a human-readable `message`,\nand, where useful, structured `details`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"code\": \"FREE_TIER_LIMIT\",\n  \"message\": \"Upgrade to translate into more languages.\",\n  \"details\": { }\n}\n```\n\nCodes in use: `VALIDATION_ERROR` (400), `UNAUTHORIZED` (401, missing or invalid credentials),\n`FREE_TIER_LIMIT` / `INSUFFICIENT_CREDITS` (402, upgrade or top up to proceed), `NOT_FOUND` (404),\n`RATE_LIMITED` (429), `INTERNAL_ERROR` (500). Asynchronous job failures surface as webhook\n`reason` values instead: `INSUFFICIENT_CREDITS`, `FREE_DURATION_LIMIT`. New codes may be added\nover time; existing ones are never renamed. A few legacy operations still return a bare message\nstring; switch on the HTTP status first and treat `code` as a refinement.\n\nAPI-key requests are rate limited per account: **120 requests/minute** overall, and\n**10 requests/minute** for Create Media. Past the limit, requests get **429** with a\n`Retry-After` header (seconds), `X-RateLimit-Limit`, and `X-RateLimit-Remaining`. Space out\npolling loops (webhooks avoid most polling) and retry after the indicated delay.\n"},"servers":[{"url":"https://api.fluen.ai:443","description":"Inferred Url"}],"tags":[{"name":"Language","description":"This namespace contains endpoints for retrieving the supported system languages."},{"name":"Media","description":"This namespace contains endpoints to read, create, and update media objects."},{"name":"Term Base","description":"This namespace contains endpoints to manage term bases and glossary terms for workspaces."},{"name":"Track","description":"This namespace contains endpoints to export subtitle tracks and to import corrected subtitles into an existing caption track."},{"name":"User","description":"This namespace contains endpoints to read the current user details."},{"name":"Webhook Endpoints","description":"Webhook Endpoint Controller"},{"name":"Workspaces","description":"Workspace management endpoints"}],"paths":{"/api/languages":{"get":{"tags":["Language"],"summary":"Read All Languages","description":"Returns a list of all available system languages","operationId":"readLanguagesListUsingGET","responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Language"}}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/media":{"post":{"tags":["Media"],"summary":"Create Media","description":"Creates a new media entry using a publicly accessible URL to the source media file. You can also specify the languages and corresponding tasks (such as captioning or translation). The media URL must be accessible without authentication; for example, a public AWS S3 URL with a presigned token is supported. Alternatively, omit 'sourceUrl' to create the media in UPLOADING state, then upload the file directly via the 'Get raw upload URL' operation.","operationId":"createMediaUsingPOST","requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/CreateMediaDto"}}}},"responses":{"201":{"description":"Created","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Media"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/media/bulk-add-translation":{"post":{"tags":["Media"],"summary":"Bulk Add Translation","description":"Add a translation language to multiple media files at once. Responds 429 when your account has too many pending translation jobs (independent of the general rate limit); wait for jobs to finish and retry.","operationId":"bulkAddTranslationUsingPOST","requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BulkAddTranslationDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"type":"object"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/media/from-captions":{"post":{"tags":["Media"],"summary":"Create Media from captions","description":"Creates a captions-only media (no source file, no transcription) from an inline SRT of existing subtitles. Use it to translate subtitles you already have, from any source, without uploading the media file: the caption track is created COMPLETE and is immediately translatable via the add-translation endpoints. Duration is derived from the SRT timing and translations are billed on it; the imported captions themselves are free. The subtitle text must fit its timing at a realistic reading speed. Also used by the Premiere plugin to translate captions made in Premiere.","operationId":"createMediaFromCaptionsUsingPOST","requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/CreateMediaFromCaptionsDto"}}}},"responses":{"201":{"description":"Created","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Media"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/media/paginated":{"get":{"tags":["Media"],"summary":"Read Media List (Paginated)","description":"Retrieves a paginated list of media for a specific workspace with optional search. Sorted by creation date (newest first) unless a sort is given.","operationId":"readMediaByWorkspacePaginatedUsingGET","parameters":[{"name":"wid","in":"query","description":"The Workspace Id","required":true,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"page","in":"query","description":"Page number (0-indexed)","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"integer","format":"int32"}},{"name":"size","in":"query","description":"Page size","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"integer","format":"int32"}},{"name":"search","in":"query","description":"Search term for filtering by title","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"sort","in":"query","description":"Sort column: title or dateCreated. Anything else falls back to dateCreated.","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"dir","in":"query","description":"Sort direction: asc or desc (default)","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PaginatedMediaResponse"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/media/titles":{"get":{"tags":["Media"],"summary":"Read Media Titles","description":"Returns a lightweight list of all of a workspace's media (id, title, caption-track id, caption language, live translation count, and eligibility flags) for matching corrected SRT filenames to the media they belong to. Unlike the paginated read, this returns the whole workspace in one call with a small per-item payload (no full track lists). Responds 400 if wid is missing and 403 if the workspace is not readable by your account.","operationId":"readMediaTitlesUsingGET","parameters":[{"name":"wid","in":"query","description":"The Workspace Id","required":true,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"type":"object"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/media/upload-url":{"post":{"tags":["Media"],"summary":"Get raw upload URL","description":"Returns a presigned S3 PUT URL for uploading the raw source file of a media that was created with no sourceUrl (so it is still UPLOADING). The client must PUT the file to the returned 'uploadUrl' with the same 'contentType' as the Content-Type header. Once the file lands, encoding starts automatically. Used by the Premiere plugin's caption-from-audio flow.","operationId":"createUploadUrlUsingPOST","requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/CreateUploadUrlDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"type":"string"}}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/media/validate-url":{"get":{"tags":["Media"],"summary":"Validate URL","description":"Checks if a URL is publicly accessible by performing a HEAD request. Used to validate media URLs before upload.","operationId":"validateUrlUsingGET","parameters":[{"name":"url","in":"query","description":"The URL to validate","required":true,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"type":"object"}}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/media/{mediaId}":{"get":{"tags":["Media"],"summary":"Read Media","description":"Returns the details of a media object, including the tracks statuses.","operationId":"readMediaUsingGET","parameters":[{"name":"mediaId","in":"path","description":"mediaId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Media"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]},"delete":{"tags":["Media"],"summary":"Delete Media","description":"USE WITH CAUTION. This endpoint will permanently delete the media entry and all the tracks associated with it.","operationId":"deleteMediaUsingDELETE","parameters":[{"name":"mediaId","in":"path","description":"mediaId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"204":{"description":"No Content"}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]},"patch":{"tags":["Media"],"summary":"Update Media","description":"Allows selected update operations on Media items such as: Adding new translation languages, change the title, move to trash.","operationId":"updateMediaUsingPATCH","parameters":[{"name":"mediaId","in":"path","description":"mediaId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/UpdateMediaDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Media"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/workspace/{workspaceId}/termbase":{"get":{"tags":["Term Base"],"summary":"Get Default Term Base","description":"Get the default term base for a workspace","operationId":"getDefaultTermBaseUsingGET","parameters":[{"name":"workspaceId","in":"path","description":"workspaceId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/TermBase"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/workspace/{workspaceId}/termbase/{termBaseId}/change-language":{"put":{"tags":["Term Base"],"summary":"Change Language","description":"Change the language of terms or translations in a term base","operationId":"changeLanguageUsingPUT","parameters":[{"name":"workspaceId","in":"path","description":"workspaceId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"termBaseId","in":"path","description":"termBaseId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"fromLanguageId","in":"query","description":"The ID of the language to change from","required":true,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"toLanguageId","in":"query","description":"The ID of the language to change to","required":true,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/TermBase"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/workspace/{workspaceId}/termbase/{termBaseId}/export":{"get":{"tags":["Term Base"],"summary":"Export Term Base","description":"Export a term base as CSV","operationId":"exportTermBaseUsingGET","parameters":[{"name":"workspaceId","in":"path","description":"workspaceId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"termBaseId","in":"path","description":"termBaseId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"type":"string","format":"byte"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/workspace/{workspaceId}/termbase/{termBaseId}/import":{"post":{"tags":["Term Base"],"summary":"Import Term Base","description":"Import a CSV file into a term base","operationId":"importTermBaseUsingPOST","parameters":[{"name":"workspaceId","in":"path","description":"workspaceId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"termBaseId","in":"path","description":"termBaseId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"requestBody":{"content":{"multipart/form-data":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"mode":{"type":"string","description":"mode"}}},"encoding":{"mode":{"contentType":"text/plain"}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"type":"object"}},"multipart/form-data":{"schema":{"type":"object"}},"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"object"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/workspace/{workspaceId}/termbase/{termBaseId}/language/{languageId}":{"delete":{"tags":["Term Base"],"summary":"Delete Language","description":"Delete a language and all its translations from a term base","operationId":"deleteLanguageUsingDELETE","parameters":[{"name":"workspaceId","in":"path","description":"workspaceId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"termBaseId","in":"path","description":"termBaseId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"languageId","in":"path","description":"languageId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/TermBase"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/workspace/{workspaceId}/termbase/{termBaseId}/terms":{"put":{"tags":["Term Base"],"summary":"Upsert Term","description":"Create or update a term in a term base","operationId":"upsertTermUsingPUT","parameters":[{"name":"workspaceId","in":"path","description":"workspaceId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"termBaseId","in":"path","description":"termBaseId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Term"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/TermBase"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]},"delete":{"tags":["Term Base"],"summary":"Clear Term Base","description":"Delete all terms and their translations from a term base. The term base itself is kept and returned empty.","operationId":"clearTermsUsingDELETE","parameters":[{"name":"workspaceId","in":"path","description":"workspaceId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"termBaseId","in":"path","description":"termBaseId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/TermBase"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/workspace/{workspaceId}/termbase/{termBaseId}/terms/bulk":{"post":{"tags":["Term Base"],"summary":"Bulk Add Terms","description":"Add multiple source-language terms in a single request. Silently skips duplicates.","operationId":"bulkAddTermsUsingPOST","parameters":[{"name":"workspaceId","in":"path","description":"workspaceId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"termBaseId","in":"path","description":"termBaseId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BulkAddTermsDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/TermBase"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/workspace/{workspaceId}/termbase/{termBaseId}/terms/{termId}":{"delete":{"tags":["Term Base"],"summary":"Delete Term","description":"Delete a term and all its translations from a term base","operationId":"deleteTermUsingDELETE","parameters":[{"name":"workspaceId","in":"path","description":"workspaceId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"termBaseId","in":"path","description":"termBaseId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"termId","in":"path","description":"termId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/TermBase"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/tracks/download":{"post":{"tags":["Track"],"summary":"Download Tracks as Zip File","description":"Export the tracks specified in input in bulk, as a single Zip file.","operationId":"exportTracksZipUsingPOST","requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DownloadTracksDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"type":"string","format":"byte"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/tracks/{trackId}":{"get":{"tags":["Track"],"summary":"Read Track","description":"Returns a single subtitle track: language, job type, status, and timestamps, in the same shape as the 'tracks' entries embedded in a media object. Webhook 'links.track' URLs point here. Responds 404 when the track does not exist, was deleted, or is not readable by your account.","operationId":"readTrackUsingGET","parameters":[{"name":"trackId","in":"path","description":"trackId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Track"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]},"delete":{"tags":["Track"],"summary":"Delete Track","description":"USE WITH CAUTION. This endpoint will permanently delete the tracks and all the changes that have been made to it.","operationId":"deleteTrackUsingDELETE","parameters":[{"name":"trackId","in":"path","description":"trackId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"204":{"description":"No Content"}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/tracks/{trackId}/burnin":{"get":{"tags":["Track"],"summary":"Read Burn-Ins","description":"Lists the burn-in jobs for a track (with status, progress percent, and ETA) so you can poll an in-flight job started via 'Start Burn-In'.","operationId":"readBurnInListUsingGET","parameters":[{"name":"trackId","in":"path","description":"trackId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BurnIn"}}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/tracks/{trackId}/burnin/{burninId}/download":{"get":{"tags":["Track"],"summary":"Get Burn-In Download Link","description":"Returns a time-limited download URL (as a plain string body, not the video bytes) for a COMPLETE burn-in of this track. Responds 400 while the burn-in is still processing.","operationId":"getBurnInDownloadLinkUsingGET","parameters":[{"name":"trackId","in":"path","description":"trackId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"burninId","in":"path","description":"burninId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"type":"string"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/tracks/{trackId}/burnin/{videoFormat}":{"post":{"tags":["Track"],"summary":"Start Burn-In","description":"Starts an asynchronous job that burns the track's subtitles into the video, producing an MP4 (H.264) with hardcoded subtitles. This is what the web app calls an MP4 export. 'videoFormat' selects the output resolution: 'STANDARD' renders HD-ready 720p, 'HIGH' renders Full HD 1080p, 'HIGHEST' renders Ultra HD 4K, and 'ORIGINAL' keeps the source resolution (up to 4K). Formats above the source resolution upscale. The request body is optional: each style field you send overrides the track's saved style (the look shown in the web editor, seeded from the workspace defaults), and omitted fields, an empty {} body, or no body at all render the track's saved style unchanged. Responds 201 with the burn-in job, 409 with {\"error\", \"existingBurnInId\"} when one is already running for this track, 403 for free-tier accounts or missing edit permission, and 400 while the track is still processing. Track when it finishes via the 'burnin.completed' webhook or by polling 'Read Burn-Ins'.","operationId":"burnTrackUsingPOST","parameters":[{"name":"trackId","in":"path","description":"trackId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"videoFormat","in":"path","description":"videoFormat","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["HIGH","HIGHEST","ORIGINAL","STANDARD"]}},{"name":"diarization","in":"query","description":"diarization","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["DASH","LABEL","NONE"]}}],"requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/TrackStyleDto"}}}},"responses":{"201":{"description":"Created","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ResponseEntity"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/tracks/{trackId}/export/{format}":{"get":{"tags":["Track"],"summary":"Export Track","description":"Export a track in the format specified in input. On free-tier workspaces exports respond 402 (upgrade required) and any permitted output is watermarked. The text transcript formats (TXT, DOCX, PDF) additionally accept 'layout' (PARAGRAPHS, the default, or ONE_LINE_PER_CUE) and 'timestamps' (NONE, the default, or PARAGRAPH to prefix each block with its start time).","operationId":"exportTrackContentUsingGET","parameters":[{"name":"trackId","in":"path","description":"trackId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"format","in":"path","description":"format","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["DOCX","ITT","PDF","SBV","SRT","SSA","STL","TTML","TXT","VTT"]}},{"name":"offsetMs","in":"query","description":"offsetMs","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"integer","format":"int64"}},{"name":"diarization","in":"query","description":"diarization","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["DASH","LABEL","NONE"]}},{"name":"layout","in":"query","description":"layout","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["ONE_LINE_PER_CUE","PARAGRAPHS"]}},{"name":"timestamps","in":"query","description":"timestamps","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["NONE","PARAGRAPH"]}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"type":"string","format":"byte"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/tracks/{trackId}/import":{"post":{"tags":["Track"],"summary":"Import Track Content","description":"Replaces the subtitles of an existing **CAPTION** track with the inline SRT in the request body, and (with `clearTranslations`) regenerates its translations.\n\nTypical use: after correcting an AI transcription outside Fluen, re-import it here. The SRT is validated and applied in a single call; an invalid SRT is rejected with `422` and nothing is written.\n\n**Parameters**\n\n- `validateOnly` (default `false`): validate the SRT without writing it, a dry run, e.g. to pre-check a batch before committing any of it.\n- `clearTranslations` (default `false`): clear the content of all the media's translation tracks and park them until the caption is completed.\n- `autoComplete` (default `false`, requires `clearTranslations=true`): mark the caption COMPLETE after the import and start all translations immediately. Re-run translations are billed like any translation. Under heavy translation load the response returns `translationsDeferred=true` and the translations stay parked; retry the same call later.\n\n**Responses**\n\n- `404`: unknown or inaccessible track\n- `422`: invalid SRT content\n- `402`: free-tier workspace","operationId":"importTrackUsingPOST","parameters":[{"name":"trackId","in":"path","description":"trackId","required":true,"style":"simple","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"validateOnly","in":"query","description":"Validate the SRT without writing it (dry run). Defaults to false: the import is applied.","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"boolean"}},{"name":"clearTranslations","in":"query","description":"clearTranslations","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"boolean"}},{"name":"autoComplete","in":"query","description":"autoComplete","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"boolean"}}],"requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ImportTrackSrtDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ResponseEntity"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/users/self":{"get":{"tags":["User"],"summary":"Read Current User","description":"Returns the account behind the credentials: id, display name, subscription plan, remaining credits ('credits' + 'creditsTopUp'), and lifetime media count. Use it to verify a key and to check balance before submitting jobs.","operationId":"readCurrentUserUsingGET","responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/User"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/webhook-endpoints":{"get":{"tags":["Webhook Endpoints"],"summary":"List your webhook endpoints","operationId":"listUsingGET","parameters":[{"name":"authenticated","in":"query","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"boolean"}},{"name":"authorities[0].authority","in":"query","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"credentials","in":"query","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"object"}},{"name":"details","in":"query","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"object"}},{"name":"principal","in":"query","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"object"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EndpointResponse"}}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]},"post":{"tags":["Webhook Endpoints"],"summary":"Register a webhook endpoint","description":"Returns the endpoint including its signing secret. The secret is shown only in this response (and after rotate-secret); use it to verify the X-Fluen-Signature header on deliveries. Each user can have at most 50 active endpoints; past that, creation responds 400.","operationId":"createUsingPOST","parameters":[{"name":"authenticated","in":"query","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"boolean"}},{"name":"authorities[0].authority","in":"query","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"credentials","in":"query","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"object"}},{"name":"details","in":"query","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"object"}},{"name":"principal","in":"query","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"object"}}],"requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EndpointRequest"}}}},"responses":{"201":{"description":"Created","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"type":"object"}}}}},"security":[{"X-API-Key":[]}]}},"/api/webhook-endpoints/sample-events":{"get":{"tags":["Webhook Endpoints"],"summary":"Sample events of a given type for field mapping","description":"Returns up to 3 recent real events of the requested type for your account (newest first), in the exact shape delivered to endpoints. Falls back to one canned example when you have no such event yet. Powers Zapier's sample-data step at Zap-setup time.","operationId":"sampleEventsUsingGET","parameters":[{"name":"authenticated","in":"query","required":false,"style":"form","schema":{"type":"boolean"}},{"name":"authorities[0].authority","in":"query","req